Original commit body from 544aff9d61d95a581cc2ee985b11359bb7baedde:

Two hypergumbo runs sharing one cache could both pick the same entry to
evict. The loser hit FileNotFoundError on the entry, the shared
`.zip.partial`, or the `.evicting-` scratch name, and the traceback
failed a run whose results were already written.

- partial archives are per-process (`<stem>.zip.<pid>.partial`)
- an entry, partial or scratch that vanished under a concurrent run is
  treated as the other run's job and skipped
- `cmd_run` calls `_housekeep_cache`, which turns any housekeeping
  exception into a stderr warning; eviction is best-effort by contract

